;
;Measurement log file c:\ke5fx\ti\HP_5370B_floor.tim
;Written by TimeLab 0.902 of Oct 29 2010 by John Miles, KE5FX (jmiles@pop.net)
;
;Field definitions:
;
;  CAP: Caption text
;  NOT: Additional notes
;  TIM: Time/date of creation
;  IMO: Instrument model
;  IRV: Instrument revision
;  IAD: Instrument address
;  ISU: Instrument setup notes
;  IFN: Filename from which data was imported, if any
;  AOP: Original acquisition option
;
;Data descriptor tags
;
;  PER: Sampling period in seconds, which also defines the left end of the tau axis
;  NOM: Nominal frequency (needed for phase unwrapping)
;  DAQ: Data acquisition rate in samples/second
;  DEN: # of output bins per tau decade
;  MIN: Min # of points required to consider bin's data valid
;  HIS: # of bin arrays (0=continuous, 1=one-shot, 2...N=N historical data sets)
;  WIN: Bin window size (initially TIC/HIS, but retains its size if acquisition truncated)
;  MJD: Modified Julian Date at beginning of run
;  DTP: DURATION_TYPE originally specified by user
;  DUR: Duration value of type DTP originally specified by user
;  STP: STOP_CONDITION originally specified by user
;  UAS: Acquisition server option
;  USP: Acquisition server port
;  UNF: Acquisition numeric field #
;  UEC: Acquisition EOS character
;  URE: Acquisition file content option
;  UAT: Acquisition auto-interval option
;  UHP: Acquisition data format option
;  UDT: Acquisition data type option
;  USC: Acquisition scale factor
;  UNW: 0=TIC data needs to be phase-unwrapped; 1=data is already unwrapped
;
;  FMD: FFT scale max dBm
;  FND: FFT scale min dBm
;  FMO: FFT scale max offset Hz
;  FNO: FFT scale min offset Hz
;  PMD: PN scale max dBc/Hz
;  PND: PN scale min dBc/Hz 
;  PMO: PN scale max offset Hz
;  PNO: PN scale min offset Hz 
;  PNB: Indirect PN calibration beatnote dBm
;  PNL: Indirect PN LNA gain dB
;  PNT: Indirect PN phase-detector gain dB
;  PNH: PN additional system gain dB
;
;  FCS nch nst: FFT channel count (0-FFT_MAX_CHANS), stored negative if real-only, 
;               followed by FFT stage count (0-FFT_MAX_STAGES)                     
;
;  FFT n_points p0 p1 XPN_n:
;               For each point:
;                 offset_Hz XPN_I XPN_Q, one line per point
;                 dBm dBc/Hz, one line per channel
;
;Data block header tags (must appear after fields above)
;
;  TIC: # of time-interval data points that follow (which determines tau range as well)
;
;Optional cached calculations (must appear after fields above): # of entries in each
;block must conform to DEN and data block size; # of instances of each block must
;be data block size / HIS
;
;  OAD: Overlapped ADEV cache entries follow
;  OHD: Overlapped HDEV cache entries follow
;  OMD: Overlapped MDEV cache entries follow
;  OTD: Overlapped TDEV cache entries follow
;

